        <div style="font-size: 20px; color: #0e1c42; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 10px;">When the Comanche were gone from the Plains, the grass was still there. So were the questions of who would use it, and how.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 18px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65;">After 1875, the Texas frontier changed quickly. Land that no Texan had dared to settle was suddenly open. You will see what changed for the Rangers, for Native Texans, and for the land itself, and what problem stood in the way of settling the dry plains.</div>
